 "sources": [
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/content/dam/boeing/v2/airports/acaps/727.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, 727 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (D6-58324, June 1978, revised May 2011), 2.2 General Dimensions: Model 727-200, 2.3 Ground Clearances, 2.4 Interior Arrangements: Model 727-200, 2.7 Door Clearances: Models 727-100, -100C and 727-200, 7.2.2 Landing Gear Footprint: Models Advanced 727-200 and -200F; 2.2 plan's flap, aileron and leading-edge lines; 3.2 C.A.R. Takeoff Runway Length (flaps 5-25); 3.3 C.A.R. Landing Runway Requirements, 30 and 40 Flaps",
   "accessed": "2026-11-24",
   "note": "The 727-200F's measured shape (shapes/B722.json; tools/trace/b722/) with the passenger aircraft's windows and doors (tools/trace/b722-passenger/derive.py). Outline, wing, tail and engines as the freighter's: read off 2.2's side, plan and front views, a 1978 scan on graph paper scaled by the printed 41.50 m to the tail cone; the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The tail's edges are straight lines and fitted curves through the scan's line centres (tools/trace/b722/straighten.py). Its crown, belly and width along the cabin are set to their least-squares lines (the scan steps 2-4 cm). Doors: the entry door (left), forward galley service door (right) and lower-deck cargo doors (right) at 2.7's 727-200 table, as on the freighter; the two Type III overwing exits each side (20 by 38 in, 2.4); the aft service doors each side (2.4, Type I; 0.76 by 1.52 m, 2.7; at 29.47 m by the photo of N555PS, where 2.7 prints 29.6 and 2.2 draws 29.25; the sill from 2.7's ground-to-sill heights against the entry door's). The window row's count and spacing from two side-on photos (the other sources), 2.2's drawn row agreeing within a window. Gear: 2.2's nose gear 4.6 m from the nose, its 19.28 m wheelbase and 5.72 m track (7.2.2 agrees); 7.2.2's tire sizes (32 x 11.5 nose, 50 x 21 main, the Advanced -200's; the first -200s had 49 x 17 mains) and spacings (0.61 m, 0.86 m). The ground is 3.21 m below the centerline: the mean of 2.3's -200 crown (L), forward and mid-fuselage bottoms (B, F), fin (J) and wingtip (K) less each part's height in the shape (3.09-3.46 m, the fin the outlier). No view in the document draws the flap track fairings; they're the 727-200F's (the same wing), measured on the photos below. Flaps and leading-edge devices: their spans and chords read off 2.2's plan (dashed under the inner wing's leading edge, the Krueger flaps; a strip along the outer wing's, the slats), settings off 3.2's and 3.3's charts."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Air_Lines_N819EA,_Las_Vegas_-_Harry_Reid_International,_October_1982.jpg",
   "title": "Eastern Air Lines N819EA, Las Vegas - Harry Reid International, October 1982 (Leslie Snelleman, CC BY-SA 4.0)",
   "accessed": "2026-11-24",
   "note": "A 727-225 from its left side, near side-on. Scaled by the door table's entry and aft service doors' middles: 26 windows behind the entry door, the two overwing exits with 2 between, 13 and two blank (Eastern's), the aft door. The row's height and the windows' size. Measured, not copied. The fairings' depth (only measurements are taken): side-on, flaps up, their aft ends show below the wing's lower edge at 26.2-26.9 m from the nose, about 0.45 m down (to perhaps 0.15 m either way: the camera is a little above the wing)."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piedmont_Airlines_Boeing_727-200_Silagi-1.jpg",
   "title": "Piedmont Airlines Boeing 727-200 N555PS (Richard Silagi, GFDL)",
   "accessed": "2026-11-24",
   "note": "From its right side, side-on. Scaled by the door table's galley service door and forward and optional aft cargo doors (agreeing within 0.06 m): from the back, a window behind the aft door, the door, 15 windows, the exits with 2 between, 21 and the blank stretch to the galley door. Measured, not copied."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G-OSRB_Boeing_727-200_T2_Aviation.jpg",
   "title": "G-OSRB Boeing 727-200 T2 Aviation, from below, 14 June 2015 (Paul Lucas, CC BY 2.0)",
   "accessed": "2026-11-26",
   "note": "The flap track fairings, measured (only measurements are taken): a 727-2S2F(Adv) seen from almost straight below, both wings, flaps up. Each wing's root and tip corners (the shape's plan) fix a projective map from the photo to the plan; four canoes a wing, their ends mapped to y and x. The two wings agree within 0.4-0.7 m in y; the fairings are their means. Their width is from the same photo (0.33-0.40 m). Two smaller fairings a wing (at the flap gap and the aileron) are left out."
  },
  {
